From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brad Barnett <127794626+bdbarnett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 07:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] esp32: A task lent a priority is scheduled at once.

When a task waits for a mutex, FreeRTOS lends its priority to the mutex's
holder. On a chip with two cores, ESP-IDF's xTaskPriorityInherit() moves a
holder that is ready to run into the ready list of its new priority and
does nothing more. If the holder is pinned to the other core, and a task of
the holder's old priority is running there, that core is never told to
choose again: its tick shares time only between tasks of the running task's
priority, and the holder has just left that list. The holder stays off the
CPU until the running task blocks or yields by itself, and the task that
lent the priority waits with it.

On an ESP32-P4 the main thread, cut off by a time slice while it held a
mutex, stayed off the CPU for 50 to 90 ms at priority 7 or 21, while a
second Python thread at priority 1 computed a TLS handshake on the same
core without the GIL. A USB host task and an audio task on the other core
waited for it that long.

Wrap xTaskPriorityInherit() at link time: once a priority has been lent,
each other core the holder may run on and isn't running on is asked to
choose its task again. A chip with one core is unchanged.
---
diff --git a/ports/esp32/esp32_common.cmake b/ports/esp32/esp32_common.cmake
index 376b393f9..baa037c3e 100644
--- a/ports/esp32/esp32_common.cmake
+++ b/ports/esp32/esp32_common.cmake
@@ -144,6 +144,7 @@ list(APPEND MICROPY_SOURCE_PORT
     modesp32.c
     machine_hw_spi.c
     mpthreadport.c
+    mutexholder.c
     machine_rtc.c
     machine_sdcard.c
     modespnow.c
@@ -320,6 +321,9 @@ target_link_options(${MICROPY_TARGET} PUBLIC
   -Wl,--wrap=memp_malloc
   -Wl,--wrap=memp_free
 
+  # A task that inherits a priority is scheduled at once (mutexholder.c)
+  -Wl,--wrap=xTaskPriorityInherit
+
   # Enable the panic handler wrapper
   -Wl,--undefined=esp_panic_handler
   -Wl,--wrap=esp_panic_handler
diff --git a/ports/esp32/mutexholder.c b/ports/esp32/mutexholder.c
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..c38fd32fc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ports/esp32/mutexholder.c
@@ -0,0 +1,81 @@
